-- title:
--   Rational mesh for the Gaussian dual integral on $[0,8]$
-- statement:
--   The 201 rational nodes cover $[0,8]$ with a finer mesh near zero. Each carries outward bounds for the density, the Hermite factors and the cubic interpolation error. All node coordinates and enclosures are stored as integer multiples of $2^{-23}$.
-- source:
--   R. Saha et al., New Lower and Upper Bounds for the Grothendieck Constant, arXiv:2608.11158v2, Appendix D.3, Lemma D.4 and Eq. (57), pp. 50–52. The interpolation-based quadrature and rational certificate adapt the construction by Igor Valuev in Prove2Me submission c940ceea-7150-49f4-b2ff-e3ae1aac955b.

